idol-cuda
Copyright 2026 Suvaditya Mukherjee

This is an unofficial CUDA port of Idol (single image to 3D Gaussians) by Speri Labs. It is not affiliated with or
endorsed by Speri Labs.

It contains code derived from idol-sdk (https://github.com/speridlabs/idol-sdk, commit 8db7003),
Copyright Speri Labs, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  - native/: an op-for-op C++ (libtorch) port of idol-sdk's pipeline, models, preprocessing and writers;
  - fast/: a re-implementation of idol-sdk's sampler and decoders that imports and reuses idol-sdk's modules;
  - kernel/: fused CUDA kernels replacing op chains of idol-sdk's models;
  - space/app.py: reuses a file-fetch workaround from idol-sdk's demo/app.py;
  - assets/examples/: eight example images copied unchanged from idol-sdk's demo/examples.

native/third_party/libwebp-1.6.0 contains parts of libwebp (https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libwebp),
Copyright Google Inc., under the BSD 3-Clause licence in that directory's COPYING file.

Model weights are not distributed here. Idol's weights (https://huggingface.co/speridlabs/idol) and the gated image
encoders it uses, DINOv3 (https://huggingface.co/facebook/dinov3-vith16plus-pretrain-lvd1689m) and the FLUX.2-dev VAE
(https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-dev), are downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub at run time and are
governed by their own licences.
